{"raw": {"https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=224703032_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Academic Advisor - International Students", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPosition Summary This Academic Advisor position supports primarily international graduate, and undergraduate student's by helping set and achieve academic, career, and personal goals by assisting with course selection and registration and orienting new students regarding key University systems. The Academic Advisor serves as a referral source to connect students to University services and resources that can assist them in achieving their goals. The Academic Advisor assists in the ongoing development and maintenance of advising resources and trainings. Through a collaborative relationship with the student, the Academic Advisor supports the student in reaching a graduation target consistent with their professional and academic goals. Application Review Date: 10/28/2026 Responsibilities: Advise a caseload of students, graduate and undergraduate, on matters including transitioning to college, registration, schedule development, goal setting, curricular and co-curricular engagement, academic progress, referral to services, and issues impacting persistence.\u00a0 Collaborate with Academic Affairs, Academic Units, Registration, and other campus resources to support advising relevant processes, procedures and work flows, including but not limited to student-centric course schedule development. Conduct early alert outreach and academic support to students. Coordinate and execute special topic workshops that support the needs of students. Serve as a liaison to academic areas, faculty mentors, financial aid, registrar, admissions, housing, access services, tutoring, writing center, and other campus resources. Collaborate with these areas to improve student success and persistence.\u00a0 Maintained detailed records and communicate regularly with faculty mentor and student on issues related to positive academic progress. Abide by FERPA regulations to uphold students\u2019 privacy.\u00a0 Develop, maintain, and promote academic advising relevant resources, which may include social media platforms, website content, student success resources, and print materials for campus stakeholders. This includes student, faculty, and staff resources and training expectations.\u00a0 Additional tasks may include committee work to support institutional priorities, departmental supports to support student success. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Qualifications: Master's Degree in Academic Advising, Higher Education Administration, Education, Student Affairs, Psychology, Social Work, or other related degree. 3-5 years\u2019 experience in the field Prior experience in academic advising, preferably at the collegiate level. Strong oral and written communication skills.\u00a0 Demonstrated experience working with diverse student populations in order to apply inclusive advising strategies.\u00a0 Ability to work collaboratively in a team environment.\u00a0 Multilingual skills highly preferred. Contributions to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=221243087_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Biology", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPosition Summary The Avila University College of Arts & Sciences, guided by its mission of excellence in teaching and learning and dedicated to service to the Dear Neighbor, is seeking a full-time Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Biology beginning Fall 2027. The successful candidate will teach and coordinate our anatomy and physiology courses and contribute to general biology and upper-division course offerings Responsibilities: Teach 12 credit hours per semester (24 credits annually) in anatomy and physiology, general biology, and advanced courses within the candidate\u2019s area of expertise that contribute to and strengthen existing biology and Professional Health Sciences programs. Coordinate and teach anatomy and physiology labs. Develop, coordinate, and teach a course-based undergraduate research experience within an advanced biology course. Create an environment in the classroom which facilitates effective student learning through the use of a wide range of teaching strategies. Mentor students in research as part of our honors capstone research experience. Participate in other service and student mentoring efforts for the School of STEM. Participate in service and scholarship consistent with a tenure-track position. (Note: Consideration for a non-tenure track position may be given to candidates who do not plan to maintain a scholarship agenda but who demonstrate teaching excellence and are willing to teach an adjusted courseload of 15 credits per semester/30 credits annually.) Participate in developing, implementing, and assessing Biology curriculum. Champion diversity, build an inclusive culture and learning experience, and maintain an equitable learning environment. Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Biology or a closely related discipline, completed by the date of appointment, is preferred. Applicants who have achieved All but Dissertation (ABD) status will also receive full consideration if degree completion is expected in the near future. Candidates holding a clinical doctorate (M.D., D.O., or D.C.) degree will also be considered. Postdoctoral experience is preferred. Teaching experience in undergraduate education is preferred. Strong preference will be given to candidates that have demonstrated the ability to incorporate evidence-based practices in undergraduate biology courses. Full-time faculty will be academically and experientially qualified and maintain expertise in previously mentioned areas of responsibility. Ability to work effectively with others in a wide variety of settings. Demonstrated commitment to creating a diverse, equitable, inclusive, safe, and just environment for students. Multilingual skills are highly preferred. Ability to contribute to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and promotes equity and social justice through their work. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=209377981_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Student Accounts Coordinator", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPosition Summary The Student Accounts Coordinator plays a vital role in the efficient operation of the Student Accounts Office within the university. This position primarily focuses on supporting student billing and providing exceptional customer service to students and their families. This role will focus on assisting students with inquiries and concerns regarding their financial obligations to the university. \u00a0 Responsibilities: Manage Student Accounts Office shared email inbox.\u00a0 Generate reports on the current status of customer accounts as requested. Support the university's student accounts department with assisting students and their families with inquiries related to their accounts. Develop and document procedures and policies in the student billing functions Prepare external communications, including payment due dates. Supervise the payment plan process, including reviewing and monitoring accounts and maintaining proper restriction holds on delinquent payment plans on student accounts. Assist and support students over the phone, by email, and in-person with issues related to collection inquiries and payment plan inquiries, including payment plan enrollment and cancellation. Assist with preparing internal training material for staff. Serve as the primary point of contact for students and families regarding financial matters. Respond to inquiries via phone, email, and in-person visits regarding student accounts, billing statements, payment, and financial holds. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Qualifications: Associates Degree or equivalent coursework, Bachelor\u2019s Degree preferred Proven experience providing administrative support, preferably in higher education. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. Ability to handle confidential information with discretion. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and scheduling, records, and database systems Knowledge of federal and state regulations related to student financial aid and billing preferred. Ability to work independently and as part of a team in a fast-paced environment. Multilingual skills highly preferred. Contributions to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=191376206_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Volunteer Assistant Coach", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPosition Summary The Volunteer Assistant Coach works under the supervision of the Head Coach for the program they are supporting. Individuals will primarily be assisting in the comprehensive day to day operations of this program. \u00a0 Responsibilities: Assist with team practices, in-game management, and film breakdown. Assist with scheduling, planning travel itineraries, and gameday preparations. Assist with recruiting initiatives, recruitment visits, and program fundraising. Help foster a positive and inclusive team culture based on integrity, sportsmanship, and respect. Any other duties assigned by the Head Coach. \u00a0 Qualifications: Collegiate athletics experience and/or coaching experience. Excellent communication, leadership, and interpersonal skills. Commitment to fostering a positive and inclusive team environment that prioritizes academic success and personal growth. Ability to work flexible hours, including evenings and weekends to attend meetings, practices, and other scheduled events, and travel as required. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=188912893_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Financial Aid & Enrollment Specialist", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\n\nLocation: Goodyear\n\nPosition Summary The Financial Aid & Enrollment Specialist supports students at its Goodyear, Arizona location. This position is responsible for providing student-focused support throughout the financial aid and enrollment process, with a primary focus on assisting domestic U.S. students with federal financial aid. The Specialist will guide students and families through FAFSA completion, financial aid requirements, eligibility documentation, and available funding options. The role will also support students after they have applied to Avila University by helping them complete admissions and enrollment requirements and coordinating next steps through enrollment. The ideal candidate has direct experience administering Federal Title IV financial aid programs, strong knowledge of Title IV regulations, and the ability to explain complex requirements to students and families in a clear and supportive manner. \u00a0 Responsibilities: Guide students and families through the FAFSA application and financial aid process. Assist students with FAFSA completion, required documentation, corrections, and resolution of outstanding financial aid requirements. Review FAFSA and student financial aid information to identify missing documentation, discrepancies, or eligibility issues. Counsel students and families regarding federal financial aid programs, grants, loans, scholarships, and other financing options. Process financial aid applications and support the determination and awarding of financial aid in accordance with federal regulations and University policies. Support verification, loan processing, Satisfactory Academic Progress requirements, and other financial aid processes. Review and update student financial aid records and maintain accurate documentation. Utilize applicable federal financial aid systems, including COD, NSLDS, FAFSA Partner Portal, and other institutional systems. Monitor student financial aid files and proactively follow up with students regarding outstanding requirements. Explain the potential financial aid impact of enrollment changes, withdrawals, or changes in academic status. Maintain current knowledge of federal Title IV regulations, financial aid policies, and applicable institutional procedures. Support financial aid reporting, reconciliation, audits, and compliance activities as required. Support students after an application for admission has been submitted. Assist applicants with completing outstanding admissions and enrollment requirements. Review student files for completeness and follow up regarding missing documentation. Provide students with clear information regarding admissions requirements, enrollment steps, deadlines, and next steps. Coordinate with Admissions, Registrar, Student Accounts, Academic Operations, and other departments to support a smooth student enrollment experience. Assist students in resolving administrative issues that may delay their enrollment. Support new student orientations, financial aid workshops, enrollment events, and other student-facing activities. Communicate with students through phone, email, in-person appointments, and other approved communication channels. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree or an equivalent combination of education and relevant professional experience required. Three or more years of direct financial aid experience, including financial aid packaging, federal loans, SAP, and professional judgment processes preferred. Minimum two years of experience required administering Federal Title IV financial aid programs, encompassing FAFSA completion, eligibility determination, verification, and a strong working knowledge of federal regulations. Experience with enterprise higher education platforms (such as Banner, Ellucian, Colleague, Campus Solutions, or Oracle Student Financial Planning) and previous experience supporting broader student services like admissions or student accounts preferred. Proficiency utilizing federal financial aid systems (including COD, NSLDS, FAFSA Partner Portal) and general student information systems or databases. Strong student-focused customer service and communication skills, with the ability to explain complex financial aid information clearly and manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Strong organizational, analytical, and problem-solving skills with strict attention to detail and accuracy when handling confidential financial information. Professional judgment and discretion, demonstrating the ability to interpret policies, apply regulatory requirements, and work collaboratively across departments. Ability to contribute to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students and multilingual learners, and contributes to equity and social justice through their work. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=185785274_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Assistant Men's and Women's Tennis Coach", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPosition Summary The Assistant Men\u2019s and Women\u2019s Tennis Coach is responsible for assisting all aspects of the tennis program, including recruitment, training, game strategy, academic monitoring, and fostering a culture of sportsmanship and excellence both on and off the field. The assistant coach will provide leadership, guidance, and mentorship to student-athletes while adhering to the mission, goals, and values of the university and the NAIA.\u00a0 \u00a0 Responsibilities: Develop and execute a strategic plan for recruiting talented student-athletes who align with the academic and athletic standards of Avila University. Establish and maintain relationships with high school coaches, club coaches, and other recruiting networks to identify prospective student-athletes. Manage the admissions process for recruited student-athletes, ensuring compliance with NAIA regulations and university admissions standards. Implement initiatives to support the academic success, personal development, and retention of student-athletes. Design and implement comprehensive training programs that focus on skill development, physical conditioning, and tactical proficiency. Conduct regular practices, conditioning sessions, and film review sessions to prepare student-athletes for competition. Foster a positive and competitive team environment that encourages teamwork, discipline, and sportsmanship. Provide individualized feedback and support to student-athletes to maximize their potential both athletically and academically. Develop and implement effective game strategies, formations, and tactics that capitalize on the strengths of the team and exploit the weaknesses of opponents. Scout upcoming opponents and analyze game footage to identify key trends, tendencies, and areas of opportunity. Make real-time adjustments and decisions during games to maximize the team's chances of success. Promote a culture of resilience, adaptability, and sportsmanship during competition. Ensure compliance with all NAIA rules and regulations governing recruitment, eligibility, and competition. Maintain accurate records of student-athlete eligibility, playing time, and academic progress. Collaborate with athletic department staff to coordinate team travel, equipment purchases, facility scheduling, and other administrative tasks. Manage the tennis budget responsibly, making strategic decisions to optimize resources and support the program's goals. Serve as a visible and positive representative of Avila University and the tennis program within the university community and the broader community. Participate in alumni events, community service projects, and other outreach initiatives to engage stakeholders and build support for the program. Assist with fundraising efforts to secure financial support for scholarships, facility improvements, and program enhancements. \u00a0 Qualifications: Collegiate tennis playing and/or coaching experience.\u00a0 Irregular work hours such as weekends, holidays, and evenings are to be expected. Multilingual skills highly preferred. Ability to string tennis rackets, utilizing various techniques and patterns, is preferred. Ability to contribute to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=169310832_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Student Enrollment Advisor - Spanish Fluency & Community Liaison", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-03\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY The Student Enrollment Advisor - Spanish Fluency and Hispanic Community Liaison serves as a key member of Avila University\u2019s frontline recruitment and onboarding team and as the University\u2019s primary admissions liaison to Spanish-speaking prospective students, families, schools, community organizations, and community partners. This position is responsible for guiding prospective students from initial inquiry through enrollment while ensuring a responsive, informative, and student-first experience. Working in a fast-paced and goal-driven environment, the Advisor executes outreach campaigns, builds strong relationships with students and families, and manages an assigned caseload to support application completion, onboarding progress, and first-day readiness. A central responsibility of this position is expanding Avila University\u2019s engagement with the Spanish-speaking community. The Advisor will communicate Avila University\u2019s admissions requirements, academic opportunities, financial aid information, enrollment processes, and student resources in Spanish; represent the University at high schools, community organizations, college fairs, and other events serving Spanish-speaking students and families; and provide Spanish-language interpretation and assistance to prospective students and families visiting campus. Responsibilities: Manage a defined caseload of prospective students, guiding them through every stage of the recruitment funnel\u2014from initial inquiry through enrollment\u2014ensuring timely completion of the application, transcript submission, FAFSA, immunization records, required paperwork, housing, and other onboarding milestones. Monitor and track student progress through the application, financial aid, and onboarding process; proactively resolve barriers by collaborating with Financial Aid, Registrar, Student Life, Academic Advising, and other appropriate University offices. Engage family decision-makers by providing financial aid guidance, connecting them to campus resources, and offering support in completing all enrollment requirements. Communicate with Spanish-speaking prospective students and families throughout the recruitment and enrollment process in Spanish, ensuring that admissions requirements, deadlines, application procedures, financial aid information, enrollment requirements, and next steps are clearly understood. Present Avila University\u2019s admissions requirements, academic opportunities, financial aid information, enrollment process, campus resources, and student experience in Spanish during individual meetings, group presentations, school visits, community events, and recruitment programs. Serve as a key liaison between Avila University and the Hispanic and Spanish-speaking community, building sustained relationships that increase awareness of and access to the University. Develop and maintain relationships with high school counselors, educators, community leaders, faith-based organizations, nonprofit organizations, businesses, cultural organizations, and other groups serving Spanish-speaking students and families. Identify opportunities for Avila University to participate in high school, community, cultural, educational, and organizational events focused on Hispanic and Spanish-speaking populations. Represent Avila University at Spanish-language and bilingual recruitment programs, college fairs, high school visits, community presentations, family programs, and organizational events. Provide Spanish-language interpretation and admissions-related translation assistance for prospective students and families during campus visits, appointments, recruitment events, admitted student programs, orientation activities, and other enrollment-related interactions. Assist Spanish-speaking families in navigating University offices and connecting with appropriate representatives in Admissions, Financial Aid, Registrar, Student Life, Academic Advising, and other campus departments. Help identify communication barriers, questions, concerns, and enrollment challenges experienced by Spanish-speaking students and families and communicate those insights to University leadership and appropriate campus departments. Support the development and review of Spanish-language recruitment and admissions communications to help ensure information provided to prospective students and families is understandable, accurate, consistent, and aligned with University messaging. Travel extensively to represent the University at in-person recruitment events, including high school visits, college fairs, community programs, and corporate or military sites. Overnight and weekend travel may be required to build strong connections with students, families, and community partners. Conduct outreach through multiple channels, including phone, text, video calls, email, and in-person meetings, with personalized and timely communication aligned with University messaging. Conduct outreach in Spanish when communicating with Spanish-speaking students and families as appropriate. Maintain accurate student records in the CRM system, documenting outreach, follow-up, student interactions, community engagement, and task completion to ensure transparency and accountability. Support on-campus recruitment and yield events, including campus tours, admitted student programs, and orientation sessions, requiring regular presence on campus in addition to travel duties. Provide Spanish-language support to students and families participating in campus tours, admissions appointments, admitted student programs, orientation sessions, and other University recruitment and enrollment activities. Meet or exceed recruitment performance benchmarks, including outreach volume, application completion, deposit rates, and enrollment yield. Contribute to recruitment goals associated with Avila University\u2019s outreach to Hispanic and Spanish-speaking prospective students and families. Provide feedback and insights from travel, student interactions, community engagement, presentations, and caseload management to inform recruitment strategies and improve processes. Maintain regular communication with community partners and help identify opportunities to strengthen Avila University\u2019s visibility and relationships within Spanish-speaking communities. Complete all University-required training and adhere to protocols for data privacy, equity, compliance, and student support. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Higher Education, Marketing, Communications, or a related field required. 1\u20133 years of experience in admissions, recruiting, institutional knowledge, student-facing enrollment services, community outreach, or a related area preferred. Professional fluency in both Spanish and English required, including the ability to speak, read, write, understand, and present information effectively in both languages. Ability to conduct individual and group admissions presentations in Spanish and clearly explain University admissions requirements, enrollment processes, financial aid information, and student resources to prospective students and families. Ability to communicate effectively with Spanish-speaking parents and family members and provide Spanish-language assistance during campus visits and enrollment-related interactions. Demonstrated ability to establish and maintain relationships with high schools, counselors, community organizations, families, and community leaders. Knowledge of or experience working with Hispanic and Spanish-speaking communities preferred. Demonstrated ability to meet and exceed performance or recruitment goals, with a proven track record of achieving metrics on a regular basis. Excellent communication and customer service skills across multiple platforms. Strong presentation, interpersonal, relationship-building, and public-speaking skills. Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage a large caseload independently. Proficiency in CRM systems, data entry, and task tracking. Ability to adapt to a fast-paced, goal-oriented environment while maintaining a student-first approach. Willingness and ability to travel locally to schools, businesses, community organizations, recruitment events, and other locations as part of recruitment and outreach activities. On-campus presence required; this is not a remote position. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively within a strong team environment. Ability to work a flexible schedule, including evenings and weekends when required for recruitment, community, and University events. Ability to contribute to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students and multilingual learners, and contributes to equity and social justice through their work. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=163056299_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Graduate Assistant - Program & Student Support (CIPGS)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPosition Summary The College of Innovative Professional and Graduate Studies (CIPGS) is seeking a dependable, professional, and student-focused graduate student to serve as a Graduate Student Assistant supporting the college's front office, student services, residency activities, and special projects. This person will serve as one of the first points of contact for students, prospective students, faculty, staff, and visitors who come to the CIPGS office. The position requires someone who is welcoming and approachable while also able to work independently, exercise good judgment, and recognize when a question or concern should be directed to a member of the CIPGS staff. In addition to front-office responsibilities, the graduate assistant will support activities associated with CIPGS's high- and low-residency programs. Responsibilities may include assisting with student arrival and check-in, intake activities, preparing materials and packets, setting up meeting spaces, greeting students and faculty, and providing logistical support during residency activities. The position will also provide opportunities to assist with college and program projects based on the student's skills, knowledge, and interests and the needs of the college. These projects may include administrative support, event preparation, communications, data organization, research, or other activities that contribute to the work of CIPGS. The ideal candidate is friendly without needing to be constantly supervised, confident enough to help people find answers, and thoughtful enough to know when to ask for help. The student should enjoy interacting with people, pay attention to details, and be willing to step away from routine front-office responsibilities to contribute to projects and activities that support CIPGS. \u00a0 Responsibilities: Serve as a welcoming and professional first point of contact for current and prospective graduate students, faculty, staff, and visitors to the CIPGS office. Provide basic information and directions and help students and visitors connect with the appropriate CIPGS staff member or university office. Assist students with navigating university resources and systems. Help students understand where to go or whom to contact when questions fall outside the scope of the graduate assistant's responsibilities. Maintain an organized, welcoming, and professional front-office environment. Assist with routine administrative and office tasks as needed. Assist with preparation for high- and low-residency activities. Help prepare student packets, materials, meeting spaces, and other resources. Assist with student arrival, check-in, and intake activities. Greet and assist students participating in residency activities. Provide logistical support to faculty and staff during residency events and meetings. Assist with other activities designed to create a welcoming and well-organized experience for residency students. Assist CIPGS faculty and staff with special projects and initiatives. Contribute to programmatic or college-level projects based on the student's skills, knowledge, and interests. Assist with event preparation, communications, data organization, research, or other projects as assigned. Handle student, faculty, program, and institutional information in accordance with university confidentiality, FERPA, and data privacy expectations. Identify appropriate tasks and take initiative during periods when front-office activity is limited. Performs additional job-related duties and responsibilities as requested. \u00a0 Qualifications: Admitted to and enrolled in an Avila University graduate program.\u00a0 Current Avila University student in good academic and conduct standing. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. Professional, welcoming, and comfortable interacting with a diverse population of students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Strong attention to detail. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise appropriate judgment. Ability to work independently and take initiative. Reliable and able to manage responsibilities with minimal supervision. Comfortable learning and using university technology and systems. Successful candidates should showcase their work and experience in contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=145458603_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Graduate Assistant - Student Success Coach", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-18\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPosition Summary The Student Success Coach Graduate Assistant works one-on-one with students who need additional academic support. The GA will help students identify challenges, develop strategies for improvement, and connect with appropriate university resources.\u00a0Tuition remission for 12 graduate credit hours per academic year (6 fall, 6 spring).\u00a0 This is an in-person position requiring 220 working hours during the academic year. The weekly schedule is flexible and will be determined with the supervisor based on the GA\u2019s class schedule and departmental needs. Once established, the schedule should remain consistent throughout the semester. Responsibilities: Meet individually with students to provide academic success coaching. Help students develop skills related to: Time management and prioritization Study skills Goal setting Communicating with professors Balancing academic and personal commitments Creating plans to catch up when falling behind Building academic confidence Connect students with appropriate campus resources and support services. Provide outreach to students identified through Navigate alerts, progress reports, midterm grades, and other Student Success initiatives. Record student meeting notes and outreach in Navigate. Participate in training and meetings with the Student Success team as needed. Perform other job-related duties as assigned by supervisor.\u00a0 \u00a0 Qualifications: Must be admitted and enrolled in a graduate program at Avila University. International students are not eligible for graduate assistantships. The successful candidate for this position will possess a bachelor's degree and must maintain a minimum 3.0 GPA, a commitment to student development, higher education, creativity, vision, passion, and compassion are imperative. Strong communication and interpersonal skills Ability to work effectively one-on-one with students Strong organization and time-management skills Ability to maintain confidentiality and professional boundaries Experience working with college students is preferred but not required The Office of Student Success Graduate Assistant position involves substantial direct involvement with students and staff in various capacities, as such it is expected that the GA must conduct themselves as a professional staff member while in the office which includes dress, behavior, and attitude.\u00a0 Project assignment will be consistent with needs, interests and expertise. The GA is expected to work the appropriate number of hours based on the allotted hours stated in the Graduate Assistant policy. The term of this position is based on the availability of the successful candidate but shall not exceed two full academic years.\u00a0 Successful candidates should showcase their work and experience in contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=143568601_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Nursing Simulation and Learning Resources Technician", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-17\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPosition Summary The Nursing Simulation and Learning Resources Technician supports nursing student learning by coordinating and running simulation activities, nursing skills laboratory operations, equipment and supply management, and educational resources. This position maintains a safe, organized, and effective learning environment; supports student skill development; and manages simulation and laboratory equipment, supplies, scheduling, and develops the purchase order request for the simulation and laboratory. \u00a0 Responsibilities: Setup and operate simulation experiences, equipment, and related technologies to support student learning outcomes. Function as a standardized patient to include memorizing and recalling scenario details to ensure each student receives the same experience. Maintain confidentiality of all case materials and student performance Be a champion for realism in clinical simulation. Become and remain proficient in the operation, maintenance, and troubleshooting of simulation and laboratory technology and equipment. Maintain a clean, safe, organized, and functional simulation and clinical skills laboratory environment. Set up and break down simulation activities and laboratory exercises in a timely manner. Arrive in advance of scheduled activities to ensure equipment functionality and availability of required supplies. Collaborate with the Simulation Coordinator and faculty for laboratory scheduling.\u00a0 Provide orientation to simulation and laboratory resources, equipment, supplies, policies, and procedures for students and new faculty as needed. Maintain inventories of simulation, laboratory, and educational supplies and equipment. Monitor equipment performance and coordinate repairs, maintenance, updates, and replacements as needed. Maintain records related to equipment acquisition, warranties, manuals, maintenance, repairs, and upgrades. Research products and technologies, solicit faculty input, and prepare recommendations for the purchase of supplies and equipment. Collaborate with the Director of Nursing and Simulation Coordinator on the annual budget recommendations related to simulation and the Nursing Education Resource Center including but not limited to laboratory equipment, supplies, and educational resources. Assist in planning for the effective allocation and utilization of simulation and nursing skills laboratory resources. Participate in strategic planning initiatives related to simulation and clinical learning environments. Serve as a resource for students and faculty regarding simulation and laboratory equipment, supplies, policies, and procedures. Foster a positive, supportive, and professional learning environment. Participate in Nursing Governance Committee meetings and other departmental, college, or university committees as requested. Maintain professional competence through continuing education and professional development activities related to nursing education, simulation, and laboratory operations. Perform other duties as assigned in support of program goals and student success. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in a relevant field (e.g., Healthcare, Education, Technology) required. Simulation certification, willingness to obtain certification, or evidence of continuing education in simulation preferred. Experience with nursing simulation, skills laboratories, and healthcare education environments preferred. Effective communication and interpersonal skills. Demonstrated proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and related technology. Ability to learn and utilize learning management systems, simulation platforms, and newly implemented software. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, and external vendors. Knowledge of simulation methodologies, clinical education technologies, and nursing skill laboratory operations. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=136751481_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Graduate Assistant - Library Circulation Desk", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-11\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPosition Summary The Hooley-Bundschu Library and Learning Commons is looking for a responsible, motivated, and customer-focused individual to staff the library\u2019s circulation desk and perform tasks related to library circulation and lending. \u00a0 Responsibilities: Maintain operations at the library\u2019s main Circulation Desk. Complete circulation and collection maintenance tasks, including checking materials in and out, reshelving, shelf reading, and inventory, with accuracy and efficiency. Answer questions and connect library users with information about library resources, services, and relevant university departments. Provide basic research assistance and help library users locate print and online resources. Maintain the library's Interlibrary Loan program and complete assigned library projects. On occasion, provide direction to other student employees and assist with tracking work hours. On occasion, oversee routine library operations during designated shifts when other library staff are unavailable. Perform additional duties as assigned. \u00a0 Qualifications: Must be admitted and enrolled as a graduate student at Avila University, and be eligible for tuition remission. International students are not eligible for graduate assistantships. Availability to work a consistent daytime schedule on weekdays is strongly preferred. Excellent customer service skills, a friendly and positive attitude, and a willingness to assist a diverse community of students, faculty, staff, and guests. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Good organization and attention to detail. Familiarity with computers and Microsoft Office Suite. Familiarity with Dewey Decimal System basics (desired but not required). Good organization and attention to detail. Ability to work efficiently, accurately, independently, and as part of a team. Prior experience with library work, library management systems, and the Dewey Decimal Classification system is preferred but not required. Successful candidates should showcase their work and experience in contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=85587086_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Technology Instructors", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-20\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY Avila University is a values-based community whose members dedicate themselves to excellence in teaching and learning and who employ the highest standards of integrity, responsibility, and excellence in teaching. \u00a0The mission of the College of Innovative Professional and Graduate Studies (CIPGS) at Avila is to provide a transformative, dynamic, and accessible learning environment that empowers students to become innovative, ethical, and socially responsible lifelong learners, modern problem solvers, practitioners, and leaders in their chosen fields. \u00a0In support of the CIPGS mission, we are seeking highly qualified and motivated adjunct instructors to teach in our undergraduate and graduate distance education (online) degree programs in the areas of technology. The successful candidate will possess a combination of academic qualifications and professional experience to ensure our students receive a well-rounded education that prepares them with the knowledge, skills, and values necessary to excel in their chosen fields. Programs: Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Business Analytics, Data Science, AI, Engineering Operations, Digital Marketing, etc. Responsibilities: Develop and deliver engaging online course content that aligns with the program's learning objectives and outcomes and is delivered using the College\u2019s approved, branded course shell\u00a0 - Assess student performance through assignments, exams, and projects - Provide regular and substantive feedback connected to the course content that supports student learning and success - Maintain communication with students on a predictable and scheduled basis \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0- Follow the adopted faculty norms when teaching in the College\u2019s distance education courses - Actively participate in professional development activities provided by the College - Collaborate with other faculty members and administrators to ensure the quality and consistency of the program - Stay current with industry trends and best practices to enhance the relevance of course content Qualifications: - Doctoral degree in business or technology-related field from a regionally accredited institution (for teaching graduate-level courses) \u00a0OR - Master's degree in business or a technology-related field from a regionally accredited institution (for teaching undergraduate-level courses) AND - Relevant professional experience in careers based in areas related to technology - Demonstrated excellence in teaching and a strong commitment to student success - Proficiency in using online learning management systems and tools - Excellent communication, organizational, and time management skills - Prior experience teaching online courses at the undergraduate or graduate level - Significant professional experience as a practitioner in a technology field of work, such as leadership roles or extensive practical experience - Active participation in professional organizations and associations related to technology - Evidence of scholarly activities, such as research, publications, or presentations Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=85593426_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Sociology Instructors", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-20\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY Contracted on a per-semester basis, the position will provide direct instruction to students by teaching classes, developing course outlines, assessing student progress, and utilizing the University\u2019s assigned technology to maintain appropriate records. \u00a0Avila University is seeking adjunct instructors for sociology courses that will be held on-campus. Teaching responsibilities will include: Responsibilities: Lectures in sociology pertaining to understanding theory, social institutions, equity, and social change. Conduct all class sessions according to the assigned schedule. Provide instruction, activities, assignments, assessments, and feedback to adequately cover all objectives for the specific course(s) taught. Deliver content using effectual methods which are appropriate to students with differing abilities, levels of preparation, and cultural experience. Use Canvas Learning Management System as part of course delivery. Work effectively with criminology faculty and the School of Social Sciences Chair. Perform other duties as needed related to assigned courses. Qualifications: \u00a0Master's degree or higher in specific discipline relevant to teaching responsibilities or a Master's degree in another area with 18 credit hours of sociology graduate coursework from an accredited university/college. Ability to contribute to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Previous teaching in higher education experience preferred. Teaching experience with a diverse population preferred. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching. Multilingual skills highly preferred. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=85595940_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Radiologic Science Instructors", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-20\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY Contracted on a per-semester basis, the position will provide direct instruction to students by teaching classes, developing course outlines, assessing student progress, and utilizing the University\u2019s assigned technology to maintain appropriate records. \u00a0Avila University is seeking adjunct instructors for sociology courses that will be held on-campus. Teaching responsibilities will include: Responsibilities: Teach Radiographic Procedures I Lab course to first year Radiologic Science students Teach simulation labs for upper extremity, shoulder girdle and lower extremity. Create an environment in the classroom which facilitates student learning. Serve as a professional role model for Radiologic Science students. Motivate students to think, to question, and to critically analyze. Qualifications: Adjunct faculty will be academically and experientially qualified and maintain expertise in areas of responsibility. Degree Information: ARRT (R) Credentialed Bachelor\u2019s Degree Required Multilingual skills highly preferred. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=85572038_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Psychology Instructors (On Campus - MS in Psychology)", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-20\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY This position requires a blend of educational expertise in the classroom to ensure student understanding of psychology principles and success in the Master of Science of Psychology Program. Responsibilities: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 On Campus lecture courses for psychology at the graduate level. Must live in the Kansas City area. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Provide instruction, activities, assignments, assessments, and feedback to adequately cover all objectives for the specific course(s) taught. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Deliver content using effectual methods which are appropriate to students with differing abilities, levels of preparation, and cultural experience. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Collaborate with university faculty and school administrators to ensure alignment between coursework and assessments. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Participate in regular meetings and professional development provided by the University.\u00a0 \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Perform other duties as needed related to assigned courses. Qualifications: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Doctoral degree OR master\u2019s degree + 18 additional credit hours of graduate coursework in psychology\u00a0 \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Minimum of masters in psychology required for teaching undergraduate courses; doctorate preferred. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Teaching experience with a diverse population (preferred). \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Experience with a Learning Management System such as Canvas (preferred). \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Experience with effective methods for engaging students through online learning (preferred) \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Ability to contribute to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Multilingual skills highly preferred. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=85599923_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Psychology Instructors - Undergrad and Grad Counseling", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-20\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY We are seeking dedicated adjunct instructors to teach in our undergraduate psychology and master\u2019s counseling psychology programs. This is an opportunity for experienced professionals to share their expertise, enrich the educational experience of a diverse student body, and/or play a vital role in shaping the next generation of licensed mental health professionals. Available positions include both daytime in-person and online undergraduate courses, as well as evening in-person graduate courses. Responsibilities: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Lecture courses for undergraduate psychology and/or graduate-level counseling psychology program.\u00a0 \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Provide instruction, activities, assignments, assessments, and feedback to adequately cover all objectives for the specific course(s) taught.\u00a0 \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Deliver content using effectual methods which are appropriate to students with differing abilities, levels of preparation, and cultural experience.\u00a0 \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Perform other duties as needed related to assigned courses. Qualifications: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 For Counseling Psychology Master\u2019s Program Courses, doctoral degree OR master\u2019s degree + 18 additional credit hours of graduate coursework in psychology or clinical licensure (e.g., licensed professional counselor, master\u2019s level psychologist, etc.) is required, \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 For Undergraduate Courses, a minimum of master\u2019s in psychology required; doctorate preferred. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Teaching experience highly preferred. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=85530991_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Physics Instructors", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-20\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY The Avila University College of Arts and Sciences, guided by its mission of excellence in teaching and learning and dedicated to service to the Dear Neighbor, is actively seeking adjunct instructors in physics for multiple part\u2011time appointments for Fall 2026 and Spring 2027. The successful candidate will be able to teach in\u2011person lectures and labs for Physics Concepts, General Physics I, and General Physics II. Responsibilities: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Conduct all class sessions according to the assigned schedule. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Provide instruction, activities, assignments, assessments, and feedback to adequately cover all objectives for the specific course(s) taught. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Deliver content using effectual methods which are appropriate to students with differing abilities, levels of preparation, and cultural experiences. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Work effectively with the program Chair. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Perform other duties as needed related to assigned courses. Qualifications: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Master\u2019s degree or higher in specific discipline relevant to teaching responsibilities or a master's degree in another area with 18 credit hours of discipline graduate coursework from an accredited university/college. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Teaching experience with a diverse population (preferred). \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Experience with a Learning Management System such as Canvas (preferred). \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Experience with effective methods for engaging students through online learning (preferred) \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Ability to contribute to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=85608547_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Music and Theatre Instructors", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-20\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPosition Summary: Avila University's School of Performing Arts is seeking dynamic and experienced adjunct faculty to join our team in providing high-quality instruction in various music and theatre courses. Contracted on a per-semester basis, these positions will provide direct instruction to students by teaching classes, developing course outlines, assessing student progress, and utilizing the University\u2019s assigned technology to maintain appropriate records. Courses Overview: Theatre courses include subjects such as Stage Combat, Stagecraft, Acting, Script Analysis, Directing Principles, Dramatic Theory & Criticism, Stage Lighting, Costume Techniques, Sound Engineering, and various advanced topics in acting, directing, and theatre design. Music courses encompass Applied Voice and Piano, Music Theory, Music History, Conducting, Orchestration, Compositional Techniques, Diction, and various performance ensembles such as Avila Singers and University Singers. The program also offers interdisciplinary courses. Responsibilities: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Provide instruction in assigned theatre or music courses, including lectures, applied lessons, and interdisciplinary classes. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Develop and implement course outlines and lesson plans that align with curriculum and learning objectives. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Assess student progress and provide constructive feedback. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Provide guidance and coaching (vocal, instrumental, dance, movement, intimacy, stage combat, etc.) in assigned music or theatre co-curricular projects/productions. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Deliver content using effective methods appropriate for students with differing abilities, levels of preparation, and cultural experiences. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Conduct all class sessions according to the assigned schedule (in-person and/or online). \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Collaborate with other faculty members, the program Chair, and Production Managers to enhance the learning experience. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Engage in professional development activities to stay current in the field. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Perform other duties related to assigned courses as needed. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Remote appointments possible depending on course needs and at the discretion of the Dean. \u00a0 Qualifications: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Master\u2019s degree or higher in a specific discipline relevant to teaching responsibilities or a Master\u2019s degree in another area with 18 credit hours of discipline graduate coursework from an accredited university/college. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Demonstrated expertise in the relevant subject areas (Musical Theatre, Stage Direction, Lighting or Sound Design/engineering, Theatre or Music History, Choral Conducting, Global Music Appreciation, String Lessons, Voice, Piano, Guitar, etc.). \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Teaching experience with a diverse population (preferred). \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Experience with a Learning Management System such as Canvas (preferred). \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Multilingual skills highly preferred. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Strong communication and interpersonal skills. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Ability to work effectively in a diverse and inclusive environment. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Commitment to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributes to equity and social justice through their work. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=85582088_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Mathematics Instructors", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-20\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY The School of STEM at Avila University is seeking qualified adjunct instructors for part-time Math courses. Courses include: Lectures and/or labs for Mathematical Literacy, College Algebra, and Elementary Probability and Statistics. Responsibilities: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Conduct all class sessions according to the assigned schedule. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Provide instruction, activities, assignments, assessments, and feedback to adequately cover all objectives for the specific course(s) taught. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Deliver content using effectual methods which are appropriate to students with differing abilities, levels of preparation, and cultural experiences. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Work effectively with the program Chair. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Perform other duties as needed related to assigned courses. Qualifications: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Master\u2019s degree or higher in specific discipline relevant to teaching responsibilities or a Master\u2019s degree in another area with 18 credit hours of discipline graduate coursework from an accredited university/college. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Teaching experience with a diverse population (preferred). \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Experience with a Learning Management System such as Canvas (preferred). \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Experience with effective methods for engaging students through online learning (preferred) \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Ability to contribute to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Multilingual skills highly preferred. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=85576523_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Education (K-12 School Guidance Counselor) Instructors", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-20\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY Avila University is a values-based community whose members dedicate themselves to excellence in teaching and learning and who employ the highest standards of integrity, responsibility, and excellence in teaching. \u00a0The mission of the College of Innovative Professional and Graduate Studies (CIPGS) at Avila is to provide a transformative, dynamic, and accessible learning environment that empowers students to become innovative, ethical, and socially responsible lifelong learners, modern problem solvers, practitioners, and leaders in their chosen fields. \u00a0In support of the CIPGS mission, we are seeking highly qualified and motivated adjunct instructors to teach in our undergraduate and graduate distance education (online) degree programs in the areas of technology. The successful candidate will possess a combination of academic qualifications and professional experience to ensure our students receive a well-rounded education that prepares them with the knowledge, skills, and values necessary to excel in their chosen fields. Responsibilities: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Develop and deliver engaging online course content that aligns with the program's learning objectives and outcomes and is delivered using the College\u2019s approved, branded course shell\u00a0 \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Assess student performance through assignments, exams, and projects \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Provide regular and substantive feedback connected to the course content that supports student learning and success \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Maintain communication with students on a predictable and scheduled basis \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Follow the adopted faculty norms when teaching in the College\u2019s distance education courses \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Actively participate in professional development activities provided by the College \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Collaborate with other faculty members and administrators to ensure the quality and consistency of the program \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Stay current with industry trends and best practices to enhance the relevance of course content Qualifications: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Doctoral degree in School Counseling or a closely related field from a regionally accredited institution (for teaching graduate-level courses) preferred. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Master's degree in School Counseling or a closely related field from a regionally accredited institution (for teaching undergraduate-level courses) required. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Relevant professional experience in careers based in areas of counseling and instruction required. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Some programs will require K-12 licensure in specific content areas. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Demonstrated excellence in teaching and a strong commitment to student success \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Proficiency in using online learning management systems and tools \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Excellent communication, organizational, and time management skills \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Prior experience teaching online courses at the undergraduate or graduate level \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Significant professional experience as a practitioner in a education-related field of work, such as leadership roles or extensive practical experience \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Active participation in professional organizations and associations related to education \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Evidence of scholarly activities, such as research, publications, or presentations\u00a0 Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=85611847_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Criminal Justice Instructors", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-20\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPosition Summary: The School of Social Sciences at Avila University is seeking qualified adjunct instructors teach fully in person and/or hybrid-flex formatted criminal justice courses. Responsibilities: Lectures in courses pertaining to understanding the criminal justice system, including courts and law, victimization. Instructors also needed to teach research and social statistics. Conduct all class sessions according to the assigned schedule. Provide instruction, activities, assignments, assessments, and feedback to adequately cover all objectives for the specific course(s) taught, Deliver content using effectual methods which are appropriate to students with differing abilities, levels of preparation, and cultural experience, Use Canvas Learning Management System as part of course delivery Work effectively with sociology faculty and the School of Social Sciences Chair. Perform other duties as needed related to assigned courses. Qualifications:\u00a0 Master's degree or higher in specific discipline relevant to teaching responsibilities or a Master's degree in another area with 18 credit hours of criminal justice graduate coursework from an accredited university/college. Ability to contribute to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work Preference will be given to candidates: Previous teaching in higher education experience Teaching experience with a diverse population. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching. Multilingual skills highly preferred. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=85605157_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Communications Instructors", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-20\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPosition Summary: Contracted on a per-semester basis, the position will provide direct instruction to students by teaching classes, developing course outlines, assessing student progress, and utilizing the University's assigned technology to maintain appropriate records. \u00a0Avila's Communication department offers undergraduate studies in Advertising and Public Relations, Film and Digital Media, and Sports Communications as well as a Master of Arts in Strategic Communication. Responsibilities: Teach Fundamentals of Communication (Multicultural Communication, Interpersonal, Group Dynamics, and Public Speaking) courses in innovative, engaging ways to help students learn and create a learning environment which encourages students to attend class regularly. Apply dynamic teaching methods to current course offerings and develop a curriculum in strategic communication strategies. Assign grades and assess student progress, potential and achievement in concrete, understandable ways to ultimately help each student progress toward their degree. Lecture and teach the material presented in the course syllabus and outline in a professional and engaging manner. Maintain appropriate records in an organized, efficient manner for every individual class taught, and have this information available for students at all times. Cultivate Avila\u2019s mission of the Sisters of St. Joseph through word and action. Recognize, celebrate, and support a wide variety of cultures and unique differences among Avila\u2019s students. Qualifications: Master's degree of Arts in Communication required. Ideal candidates would possess a Public Relations or Advertising background and/or have relevant work experience in strategic communications, including social media, mobile and digital content creation, publication, and evaluation. Background in Leadership and Entrepreneurship preferred. Multi-lingual skills highly preferred. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=85679549_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Computer Science Instructors", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-20\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPosition Summary: The School of Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics (STEM) at Avila University is seeking qualified adjunct instructors teach fully in person and/or hybrid-flex formatted computer science courses. Responsibilities: Lecture courses for computer science that would include C# programming language. Lecture courses for cybersecurity that would include basic introductory concepts and regulatory compliance. Provide instruction, activities, assignments, assessments, and feedback to adequately cover all objectives for the specific course(s) taught. Deliver content using effectual methods which are appropriate to students with differing abilities, levels of preparation, and cultural experience. Perform other duties as needed related to assigned courses. Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree or higher in specific discipline relevant to teaching responsibilities or a Master\u2019s degree in another area with 18 credit hours of discipline graduate coursework from an accredited university/college. Demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching. Teaching experience with a diverse population (preferred). Experience with online learning, especially with a Learning Management System such as Canvas (preferred). Multilingual skills highly preferred. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=86150129_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Clinical Nursing Instructors", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-20\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPosition Summary: The School of Nursing at Avila University invites applications for adjunct clinical instructor positions for various placements for Spring, Summer, and Fall semesters. Clinical adjunct instructors may include the following placements (in-patient environment only): Critical Care, Medical Surgical/Telemetry, Mental Health, Pediatrics, Obstetrics (OB). Placements occur on Tuesdays, Thursdays, and Fridays. Responsibilities: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Clinical adjunct instructors may include the following placements (in-patient environment only): o \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Critical Care o \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Medical Surgical/Telemetry o \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Mental Health o \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Pediatrics (Peds) o \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Obstetrics (OB) \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Provide instruction, activities, assignments, assessments, and feedback to adequately cover all objectives for the specific course(s) taught. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Deliver content using effectual methods which are appropriate to students with differing abilities, levels of preparation, and cultural experience. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Work effectively with the program Chair and/or the Laboratory Manager. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Remote appointments possible depending on course needs and at the discretion of the Dean. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Perform other duties as needed related to assigned courses. Mentorship and Support:\u00a0 o \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Serve as a mentor and resource for student teachers, offering guidance on lesson planning, curriculum development, and instructional strategies. o \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Assist student teachers in navigating challenges encountered during their teaching placements, offering support and solutions as needed. o \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Foster a supportive and collaborative learning environment where student teachers feel encouraged to reflect on their practice and continuously improve. Collaboration and Coordination:\u00a0 o \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Collaborate with university faculty, cooperating teachers, and school administrators to ensure alignment between coursework and practical teaching experiences. o \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Coordinate logistics related to student teacher placements, including scheduling observations, arranging meetings, and facilitating communication between stakeholders. o \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Participate in regular meetings and professional development activities to stay updated on best practices in teacher education and supervision. Professional Development:\u00a0 o \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Engage in ongoing professional development to enhance expertise in educational theory, instructional methods, and assessment practices. o \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Stay informed about current trends and research in teacher education, incorporating relevant knowledge into supervision practices. o \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Pursue opportunities for professional growth and networking within the field of education. Administrative Duties:\u00a0 o \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Maintain accurate records of student teacher observations, evaluations, and progress reports. o \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Ensure compliance with licensure requirements and accreditation standards related to student teaching placements. o \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Assist in the coordination of programmatic assessments and evaluations to monitor the effectiveness of the student teaching program. Qualifications: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Master\u2019s degree in nursing o \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 BSN degree with concurrent enrollment in a Master\u2019s in nursing program may be considered. Attendance at the Clinical Faculty Academy (CFA) is required. \u00a0For information on CFA please visit https://kchealthcareers.com/clinical-faculty-academy . \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Current or past clinical expertise in designated setting. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Prior clinical teaching experience preferred. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Knowledge of or willingness to learn Canvas LMS or similar computer classroom management system. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Missouri nursing license required. \u00a0Kansas license (or multi-state license) required if clinical placement is in Kansas. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Teaching experience with a diverse population (preferred). \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Experience with a Learning Management System such as Canvas (preferred). \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Experience with effective methods for engaging students through online learning (preferred) \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Ability to contribute to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Multilingual skills highly preferred. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=86153376_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Chemistry Instructors", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-20\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPosition Summary: Avila University is recruiting for adjunct instructors in chemistry for multiple part-time appointment Responsibilities: Teaching responsibilities will include: Lectures and/or labs for Introductory Chemistry (e.g. Principle of Chemistry, General chemistry I & II) Conduct all class sessions according to the assigned schedule. Provide instruction, activities, assignments, assessments, and feedback to adequately cover all objectives for the specific course(s) taught. Deliver content using effectual methods which are appropriate to students with differing abilities, levels of preparation, and cultural experience. Work effectively with the program Chair and/or the Laboratory Manager. Perform other duties as needed related to assigned courses. Qualifications: Master's degree or higher in specific discipline relevant to teaching responsibilities or a Master's degree in another area with 18 credit hours of discipline graduate coursework from an accredited university/college. Demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching. Teaching experience with a diverse population (preferred). Multilingual skills highly preferred. Ability to contribute to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Multilingual skills highly preferred. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=86155904_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Business (Accounting and Finance) Instructors", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-20\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPosition Summary: Avila University is a values-based community whose members dedicate themselves to excellence in teaching and learning and who employ the highest standards of integrity, responsibility, and excellence in teaching. \u00a0The mission of the College of Innovative Professional and Graduate Studies (CIPGS) at Avila is to provide a transformative, dynamic, and accessible learning environment that empowers students to become innovative, ethical, and socially responsible lifelong learners, modern problem solvers, practitioners, and leaders in their chosen fields. \u00a0In support of the CIPGS mission, we are seeking highly qualified and motivated adjunct instructors to teach in our undergraduate and graduate distance education (online) degree programs in the areas of technology. The successful candidate will possess a combination of academic qualifications and professional experience to ensure our students receive a well-rounded education that prepares them with the knowledge, skills, and values necessary to excel in their chosen fields. Responsibilities:\u00a0 Develop and deliver engaging online course content that aligns with the program's learning objectives and outcomes and is delivered using the College\u2019s approved, branded course shell\u00a0 - Assess student performance through assignments, exams, and projects - Provide regular and substantive feedback connected to the course content that supports student learning and success - Maintain communication with students on a predictable and scheduled basis\u00a0 - Follow the adopted faculty norms when teaching in the College\u2019s distance education courses - Actively participate in professional development activities provided by the College - Collaborate with other faculty members and administrators to ensure the quality and consistency of the program - Stay current with industry trends and best practices to enhance the relevance of course content Qualifications:\u00a0 - Doctoral degree in accounting, finance, or a closely related field from a regionally accredited institution (for teaching graduate-level courses) \u00a0OR - Master's degree in accounting, finance, or a closely related field from a regionally accredited institution (for teaching undergraduate-level courses) AND - Relevant professional experience in accounting or finance, such as CPA, CFA, or other industry certifications - Demonstrated excellence in teaching and a strong commitment to student success - Proficiency in using online learning management systems and tools - Excellent communication, organizational, and time management skills - Prior experience teaching online courses at the undergraduate or graduate level - Significant professional experience in accounting or finance, such as leadership roles or extensive practical experience - Active participation in professional organizations and associations related to accounting or finance - Evidence of scholarly activities, such as research, publications, or presentations Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=86179319_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Biology Instructors", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-20\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPosition Summary: The School of STEM at Avila University is seeking qualified adjunct instructors for the Biological Sciences. Responsibilities: Avila University needs adjunct instructors for multiple part-time appointments. Teaching responsibilities will include: Lectures and/or labs for Introductory Biology (e.g. Cells, Genes, Ecology, Evolution, Environmental Science, Organismal Biology) or Conduct all class sessions according to the assigned schedule. Provide instruction, activities, assignments, assessments, and feedback to adequately cover all objectives for the specific course(s) taught, Deliver content using effectual methods which are appropriate to students with differing abilities, levels of preparation, and cultural experience, Work effectively with the program Chair and/or the Laboratory Manager, Perform other duties as needed related to assigned courses. Qualifications: Master's degree or higher in specific discipline relevant to teaching responsibilities or a Master's degree in another area with 18 credit hours of discipline graduate coursework from an accredited university/college. Demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching. Teaching experience with a diverse population (preferred). Multilingual skills highly preferred. Ability to contribute to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Stipend based on the credit hours assigned and previous teaching experience. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=104247430_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Landscaping Specialist", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-16\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY The Landscaping Specialist is responsible for mowing and maintaining campus grounds, basic landscaping, snow and ice removal as needed, and assisting with general facilities tasks. The position reports directly to the Director of Facilities. This individual will be responsible for leading the groundskeeping/landscaping efforts for the campus.\u00a0 Responsibilities: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Mow and trim lawns using riding and walk behind mowers, trimmers, and related equipment. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Perform basic landscaping such as weeding, mulching, raking, and general care of shrubs, trees, and flower beds. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Devise plans for seasonal planting of flowers and/or other plants.\u00a0 \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Remove snow and ice from walkways, steps, and entry areas using shovels, snow blowers, and ice melt products as directed. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Perform routine maintenance on the landscaping equipment while maintaining documented logs as needed. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Lead the effort the during off season regarding winterizing irrigation lines and fountains while communicating with contractors effectively as needed. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Keep exterior areas free of trash, debris, and other hazards to support a clean and safe campus environment. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Drive campus grounds looking for any damage to landscaping or irrigation systems and sidewalks or driveways. Reporting any damages to department leadership. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Operate and perform routine checks on grounds equipment and tools to ensure they are clean, safe, and in good working order. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Assist facilities staff with other maintenance tasks as needed, including light repairs, event setups, and special projects as assigned by the Director of Facilities. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Perform other job-related duties as assigned, including but not limited to, housekeeping and janitorial tasks as needed. Requirements: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 High school diploma or GED required. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Two (2) years of experience in landscaping or maintenance required. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Knowledge of various plant material preferred. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Knowledge of safety precautions and procedures \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Ability to navigate work order system and prioritize/delegate work tickets to facilities staff \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Ability to work independently with little direction \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Ability to meet schedules and timelines for projects and event setups \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with others \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Ability to work different hours when needed including weekends. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Ability to work in all weather conditions \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Ability to lift 50lbs repetitively \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Ability to stand, kneel and squat for long periods of time \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Must possess a valid Missouri driver\u2019s license. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, employee assistance program, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=85511602_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Graduate Assistant \u2013 Residence Life", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-16\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY The Graduate Assistant (GA) position for Residential Life\u2019s primary function is to help contribute to a robust residential life experience at Avila University by assisting in the engagement and development of students living on campus. This Graduate Assistant will gain experience in assessment, presenting, advising, and event planning for resident programming. \u00a0This position requires a flexible and variable time commitment, with hours dependent on the needs of the residential community, which includes but is not limited to: being on campus during critical operational periods, including Move-In, Move-Out, Homecoming, Open House, break closures (as assigned), and limited time away from the residential facility to such as no more than 2 weekends per month and no more than 1 night per week, with prior approval. Responsibilities: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Review, educate, and adhere to, residential policies, University policies, as well as federal, state and local law. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Enforce all federal, state, local laws, and University policies as needed according to procedures in the Avila University Student Handbook. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 General knowledge of all aspects of the Avila University Student Handbook and Student Conduct Process.\u00a0 \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Maintain a minimum GPA that maintains academic good standing, varies based on position. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Maintain full time student status, 12 credit hours for undergraduate and 6 credit hours for graduate level, each semester. \u00a0Exceptions to this policy must be reviewed and approved or denied by the Assistant Dean for Residential Life & Housing. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Assist in building operations as assigned/needed (i.e. check in, check out, inventory/maintenance reports, emergency response and training, etc.) \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Note and report maintenance concerns, and then follow up on those concerns. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Complete weekly report detailing specific information to submit to direct supervisor. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Is responsible for and takes pride in the appearance of the residential area of management and takes appropriate steps to ensure it is properly cleaned and maintained. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Maintains confidentiality regarding student records, student behavior and residence life information. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Maintains regular communication with direct supervisor and central staff as needed/appropriate. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Assists/Coordinates residential programming events as required. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Remains on campus for closed weekends, including but not limited to: Move In Day, Homecoming, Open House, Move Out Week, etc. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Spends no more than 2 weekends per month and 1 night per week away from assigned residential facility. Prior approval is required. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Attends weekly staff meetings for building/area. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Attends weekly all-staff meetings as required by central staff. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Attends regularly scheduled meeting with direct supervisor. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Participates in central staff duty weeknight and weekend rotation. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Manages emergency situations. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Remain on campus through closing at breaks and end of fall and spring semesters. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Assist in opening of residential facilities for fall and spring semesters. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Facilitate roommate/suitemate/floormate mediation as needed. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Complete lockouts as needed. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Serve as an information resource for residents. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Serve as a student advocate for residential students. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Build community within residential area. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Develop and facilitate training sessions for residence life staff. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Complete 20 office hours in Housing Office weekly. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Assist in the planning and execution of residential programs including planning, budgeting, and hosting events on a regular basis. A schedule of events will be prepared in collaboration with direct supervisor.\u00a0 \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Create a library of ideas and examples of bulletin boards and door decorations for RAs to use as a resource. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Track and maintain student staff resource room(s) items and submit requests for supplies. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Anticipate and plan for interim/break housing programming.\u00a0 \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Work closely with the international student office to gain insight and feedback in how to effectively program for international students. Inventory and maintain resource room supplies. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Perform regular walkthroughs of the residential facilities (inside and outside).\u00a0 \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Identify areas of concern and opportunity for facility use. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Review and edit facility related forms such as Room Condition Forms, maintenance requests, and residence hall signage. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Assist with campus tours. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Assist with identifying and coordinating show rooms throughout the school year. Qualifications: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Must be admitted and enrolled in a graduate program at Avila University. International students are not eligible for graduate assistantships. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 The successful candidate for this position will possess a bachelor's degree and\u00a0 must maintain a minimum 3.0 GPA, a commitment to student development, higher education, creativity, vision, passion, and compassion are imperative. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Strong interpersonal, communication, and problem-solving skills. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Ability to work collaboratively with diverse groups of students, faculty, staff, and external partners. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Demonstrated commitment to student development, diversity, equity, and inclusion. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Proficiency in using relevant technology and software for managing student services and data. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 The GA is expected to work the appropriate number of hours based on the allotted hours stated in the Graduate Assistant policy. \u00a0The term of this position is based on the availability of the successful candidate but shall not exceed two full academic years. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 It is a requirement for this role that the individual reside in a specified location in campus housing. Additionally, due to the on-call responsibilities, room and board fees will be covered by the department. Successful candidates should showcase their work and experience in contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=85464282_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Housekeeper", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-16\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY As a University Housekeeper, you will play a critical role in maintaining cleanliness, hygiene, and orderliness across the university campus facilities. You will be responsible for ensuring that academic buildings, administrative offices, dormitories, and other university premises are kept in pristine condition to create a conducive environment for learning, working, and living \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Responsibilities: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Keeping facilities and common areas are clean and maintained \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Vacuums and sweeps floors, carpet, and rugs \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Cleans and sanitizes bathrooms, showers, toilets, sinks, and countertops \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Replenishes toiletries and paper towels \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Empties trash receptacles \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Performs deep cleaning when required \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Responds to calls for housekeeping problems throughout campus \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Work with a team of housekeepers on each shift \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Monitor and report on the inventory of cleaning supplies \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Deep cleaning of dormitories annually \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Champion diversity, build an inclusive culture and learning experience, and maintain an equitable learning environment. Requirements: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Ability to lift at least 25 Ibs. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Ability to manage your time efficiently and work well under little supervision \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 High school Diploma or at least 3 years in a housekeeping or custodian position \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Evening and weekend availability required, some overtime is expected \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Multilingual skills highly preferred \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Ability to contribute to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, employee assistance program, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=236676700_25&lang=en_US": {"title": "Housekeeper (Part-Time)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY As a Housekeeper, you will play a critical role in maintaining cleanliness, hygiene, and orderliness across the university campus facilities. You will be responsible for deep cleaning projects through campus to help ensure that academic buildings, administrative offices, dormitories, and other university premises are kept in pristine condition to create a conducive environment for learning, working, and living.\u00a0 Responsibilities: Perform specialized deep cleaning of restrooms, classrooms, common areas and other assigned facilities\u00a0 Perform floor care duties, including machine scrubbing and carpet extraction as needed Perform special move-out cleaning for student housing Deep clean hard to reach and frequently overlooked areas\u00a0 Maintain cleaning equipment and supplies in a clean, organized and operational condition Champion diversity, build an inclusive culture and learning experience, and maintain an equitable learning environment Perform other housekeeping duties, as assigned Requirements: Ability to lift at least 25 lbs. Must be able to work independently and manage time efficiently with little supervision High school Diploma or 3 years in housekeeping or custodial positions Ability to work on a ladder and in tight spaces Multilingual skills highly preferred\u00a0 Ability to contribute to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributes to equity and social justice through their work Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, employee assistance program, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=233415798_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Counseling Services Clinician (Part-Time)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPosition Summary The Counseling Services Clinician, reporting to the Director of Counseling and Psychological Services, will be employed to provide counseling services to the Avila student population throughout the 2026-2027 academic year (late August through early May) on a Part-Time basis (approximately 6-8 clinical hours per week). Demonstrating student-centered philosophy in support of student success, this position provides individual counseling for Avila students, including providing emergency/crisis intervention, and making referrals to community organizations as needed for their clients. This is a remote position and is sch \u00a0 Responsibilities: Providing excellent counseling services, while demonstrating awareness of current best practices and counseling theory.\u00a0 Establishing and maintaining confidential electronic counseling files.\u00a0 Working in tandem with Director of Counseling and Psychological Services, providing consultation to Avila faculty and staff regarding student behavioral and emotional issues.\u00a0 \u00a0 Qualifications: Masters or Doctorate degree in a licensable mental health discipline (counseling, social work, psychology, etc) required. License to provide mental health counseling services in the state of Missouri (ideally Missouri and Kansas) required. Qualified applicants may include those holding licenses such as LPC, LCSW, and LP.\u00a0 Experience and/or special interest in working with college-aged population preferred.\u00a0 EMDR trained clinicians encouraged to apply.\u00a0 Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=229472844_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Executive Assistant to Provost", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY The Executive Assistant to the Provost is responsible for maintaining the smooth operation of the Academic Affairs office while overseeing and coordinating various office procedures and resources to ensure efficiency and effectiveness. This position serves as a central point of \u00a0contact for internal and external stakeholders, handling communication, logistics, and administrative tasks. Responsibilities: Assist the Provost in the day-to-day operations of the Academic Affairs Office: This includes overseeing office communication, planning and organizing meetings, managing scheduling tasks, and performing other essential administrative duties to ensure smooth operations within the Academic Affairs Office. Serve as the initial contact point for Academic Affairs, including assisting students and other internal and external constituents with questions and concerns related to academic policies, processes, and experiences. Lead the coordination and logistics for academic ceremonies, including annual commencement ceremonies. Maintain faculty files and prepare and track records for annual faculty contracts and appointment letters. Assist in the management of academic budgets and the preparation of budget reports, including processing payroll memos for faculty stipends, invoices, and reimbursement requests, as needed. Collaborate with the Vice President of Academic Affairs and the Registrar in developing and maintaining the academic calendar. Collaborate with the HR department in faculty and staff hiring and orientation processes. Work with academic leaders across campus to facilitate the approvals of affiliation agreements and MOUs that require the Provost\u2019s signature. Compile submissions from leaders on the Provost\u2019s Leadership Team into a single report for each Board of Trustees meeting (four times per year), editing as needed to ensure consistent voice and formatting. Facilitate administrative functions for the Provost: This includes coordinating and scheduling appointments and meetings, reserving facilities for events, maintaining the Provost\u2019s calendar, and preparing and distributing various event calendars to ensure all logistical needs are met efficiently. Provide administrative support to key university committees, including IRB, Faculty Scholarship Committee, and Rank & Tenure Committee, ensuring that files and recommendations are properly routed in a timely and consistent manner. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s Degree or equivalent coursework required. Proven experience as an Office Manager or similar administrative role required; prior executive support experience in higher education preferred. Excellent communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills. Proficiency in office software applications (e.g., Microsoft Office Suite). Strong attention to detail and organizational, multitasking, and problem-solving skills. Ability to handle confidential information with discretion. Ability to prioritize tasks, work independently, and meet deadlines. Multilingual skills highly preferred. Ability to contribute to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=229282928_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Dissertation Development and Research Support Coordinator", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPOSITION \u00a0 SUMMARY The Dissertation Development and Research Support Coordinator provides academic leadership, faculty mentorship, research consultation, and quality assurance across the dissertation process. The Coordinator supports faculty serving as Dissertation Chairs and provides candidates and chairs with guidance on research design, methodology, analysis, and ethical research practice. This role promotes consistent scholarly standards, strengthens faculty capacity, and supports timely progression through dissertation milestones. The Coordinator serves as a program-wide resource, supplementing the work of faculty advisors and dissertation chairs and committees. This is a full-time faculty administrator position with faculty rank. Responsibilities: Mentor and support faculty serving as Dissertation Chairs, particularly new and first-time chairs.\u00a0 Provide guidance on dissertation supervision, substantive feedback, candidate progression, and milestone management.\u00a0 Facilitate professional development related to dissertation advising, research methodology, ethical practice, and scholarly standards.\u00a0 Help chairs identify appropriate methodological expertise for a candidate\u2019s dissertation committee or for targeted consultation.\u00a0 Provide consultation to candidates and chairs on research questions, design, methods, data collection, analysis plans, and interpretation of findings.\u00a0 Assist candidates in evaluating the feasibility and scope of proposed project-based dissertations in coordination with their Faculty Advisor or Dissertation Chair.\u00a0 Support chairs and candidates in identifying appropriate research resources, tools, and specialized expertise.\u00a0 Refer methodological or subject-matter questions beyond the Coordinator\u2019s expertise to a qualified specialist, as needed.\u00a0 Guide candidates and chairs in understanding research ethics and preparing for IRB review, while recognizing that formal IRB determinations rest with the appropriate institutional body.\u00a0 Promote consistency in dissertation expectations, evaluation criteria, and scholarly rigor across Dissertation Chairs and committees.\u00a0 Review dissertation proposals or drafts as needed to advise on alignment with program standards and identify areas requiring further attention by the Chair and committee.\u00a0 Advise chairs on addressing common dissertation challenges involving scope, methodology, candidate readiness, or the coherence of the project.\u00a0 Contribute to consistent use and refinement of dissertation policies, templates, rubrics, and assessment tools.\u00a0 Assist with program-level coordination related to dissertation enrollment, milestones, review processes, and completion timelines.\u00a0 Monitor patterns in candidate progression and dissertation completion to identify support needs and opportunities for program improvement.\u00a0 Provide feedback to the Ph.D. Program Director regarding dissertation processes, faculty workload, methodological support needs, and resource requirements.\u00a0 Serve as a consultative resource when chairs encounter complex methodological, ethical, or progress-related issues.\u00a0 Support chairs in navigating IRB institutional research policies and dissertation procedures.\u00a0 Assist the Ph.D. Program Director and chairs in addressing concerns related to candidate progress, timeline delays, or academic standards.\u00a0 Collaborate with the Program Director, Faculty Advisors, Dissertation Chairs, committee members, and academic leadership to ensure coherent support across dissertation stages.\u00a0 Communicate research support opportunities and dissertation process expectations clearly to candidates and Dissertation Chairs.\u00a0 Maintain appropriate records of consultations and program-level issues to support continuity and improvement.\u00a0 Teach courses and serve as Dissertation Chair for select students in the PhD program as needed, subject to appropriate faculty qualifications and program needs.\u00a0 Qualifications: Earned research-based doctoral degree (PhD or equivalent) from a regionally accredited institution.\u00a0 Expertise in doctoral research design and methodology, including applied or project-based dissertations. \u00a0A minimum of three years\u2019 experience teaching at the graduate level required; doctoral-level teaching experience is preferred.\u00a0 A record of teaching and scholarship appropriate for rank appointment at the level of Associate Professor or higher. Proven successful experience serving as a doctoral Dissertation Chair and/or dissertation committee member.\u00a0 Knowledge of qualitative, quantitative, and mixed methods research approaches sufficient to consult on methodological fit and identify when specialized expertise is needed.\u00a0 Familiarity with institutional dissertation standards, Institutional Review Board (IRB) processes, and ethical research practices.\u00a0 Ability to assess the alignment among a candidate\u2019s problem, research questions, design, data collection, analysis, and intended applied contribution.\u00a0 Ability to recognize questions beyond the Coordinator\u2019s expertise and refer candidates and chairs to a qualified methodological or subject-matter specialist.\u00a0 Experience in faculty mentoring, academic leadership, or program oversight.\u00a0 Demonstrated experience providing methodological consultation on qualitative, quantitative, or mixed methods projects.\u00a0 Evidence of effective interpersonal, coaching, facilitation, and communication skills, including the ability to support doctoral candidates and faculty in an online program. Ability to contribute to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=229273954_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Program Director, Ph.D. in Strategic Leadership and Innovation", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY The Director of the Ph.D. In Strategic Leadership and Innovation provides strategic, academic, and operational leadership for the doctoral program, ensuring alignment with institutional mission, accreditation requirements, and standards for doctoral-level rigor. The Program Director oversees curriculum quality, faculty engagement, student progression, and program outcomes, with particular attention to maintaining high-quality online delivery consistent with Regular and Substantive Interaction (RSI) expectations and doctoral best practices. This role ensures the coherence of the program from admission through dissertation completion, coordinating across Faculty Advisors, Dissertation Chairs, and institutional leadership. Responsibilities: Provide overall leadership for the doctoral program, ensuring alignment with institutional mission and strategic priorities. Oversee program design, implementation, and continuous improvement. Monitor program coherence across admission, coursework, advising, and dissertation phases. Oversee curriculum development, review, and revision to maintain academic rigor and relevance. Oversee alignment of course outcomes with program learning outcomes and dissertation expectations. Maintain quality and consistency in online delivery, including compliance with RSI and distance education standards. Recruit, appoint, and evaluate doctoral faculty, including Faculty Advisors and Dissertation Chairs, in accordance with the faculty handbook and in collaboration with deans and other program directors. Review faculty qualifications for alignment with institutional requirements and accreditation standards. Support faculty development related to teaching, advising, and dissertation supervision. Monitor faculty workload, including dissertation supervision capacity, to maintain appropriate student-to-faculty ratios. Lead cohort onboarding and orientation and build a community of scholars among Ph.D. students. Review student progression across all program stages, including coursework, milestones, and dissertation completion. Ensure effective advising structures are in place to support timely completion of coursework and program milestones. Address student concerns, appeals, or progression challenges with guidance from the Dean of the College of Innovative and Professional Studies (CIPGS). Lead implementation of the dissertation framework, including coordination among Faculty Advisors, Dissertation Chairs, and the Coordinator of Dissertation Development & Research Support. Monitor dissertation progress, completion rates, and time-to-degree. Support continuous improvement of dissertation policies, processes, and assessment tools. Coordinate program assessment, including evaluation of student learning outcomes and program effectiveness, working with the Director of Assessment, as needed. Maintain program-level evidence and compliance and provide data and narrative for institutional reports in coordination with the CIPGS Dean and University Accreditation Liaison Officer. Oversee scheduling, course staffing, and program budgeting. Collaborate with enrollment, marketing, and student support services to ensure effective recruitment and retention strategies. Maintain program data related to enrollment, retention, completion, and faculty performance. Serve as the primary liaison between the doctoral program, academic administration and university leadership. Collaborate with Academic Affairs, institutional research, and support units to ensure program effectiveness. Communicate program expectations, updates, and outcomes to faculty and stakeholders. Qualifications: Earned terminal doctorate from a regionally accredited Institution with a documented record of scholarship; Ph.D. preferred. Expertise in leadership, innovation, or a field aligned with the doctoral program. Demonstrated knowledge of doctoral education, research design, and applied/project-based dissertations. Familiarity with accreditation standards (e.g., Higher Learning Commission) and distance education regulations; Experience with RSI standards preferred. Understanding of curriculum design, assessment, and program evaluation at the graduate/doctoral level. 10+ years experience teaching at the graduate level required; at least some experience teaching or overseeing dissertation work for doctoral students. A record of teaching and scholarship at the rank of Associate Professor required; earned rank of Professor preferred. Demonstrated expert knowledge of doctoral dissertation supervision, including dissertation processes, standards, and evaluation at the doctoral level. Demonstrated academic leadership experience (e.g., program director, department chair, or equivalent). Experience in online program delivery, faculty supervision, and student success initiatives. Evidence of scholarly activity is required; applied professional leadership experience is preferred. Experience serving adult and working-professional learners is preferred. Successful candidates should be committed to contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. Benefits: This is a full-time position, eligible for the usual and customary benefits. Avila University\u2019s comprehensive benefit package includes a generous holiday schedule, tuition remission for employee and dependents, vacation and sick leave, retirement benefits and health insurance.\u00a0 The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities. \u00a0Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law. \u00a0 You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)\u201d and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.", "department": ""}}, "rows": {"https://workforcenow.c